#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:98
#: 94d3320b3ee24812a73b05a6c76f91b0
msgid ""
"The `ArduPilot firmware server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__ provides"
" pre-compiled firmware for a wide range of boards and configurations.  The "
"core dev team diligently maintains the server including applying security "
"patches and updates.  However, if you want to be sure that the code running "
"on your autopilot is exactly the code you have reviewed, consider "
":ref:`building the code yourself <building-the-code>`."
msgstr ""
"`ArduPilot 固件服务器 <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__ "
"为众多飞控板和配置提供预编译固件。核心开发团队勤勉地维护该服务器，包括应用安全补丁和更新。但是，如果您想确保飞控上运行的代码与您审查过的代码完全一致，可以考虑"
" :ref:`自行构建代码 <building-the-code>`。"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:101
#: 979924a817fc42368162ca92ec9f8525
msgid "Reporting Security Issues"
msgstr "报告安全问题"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:103
#: dcd16e2b42ec4dc298fd818b69261169
msgid ""
"If you believe you have found a security issue in ArduPilot, please raise an"
" issue in the `issues list "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues>`__ and optionally post a "
"link to the issue in the :ref:`ArduPilot Discord Server's <ardupilot-"
"discord-server>` \"code_review\" channel."
msgstr ""
"如果您认为在 ArduPilot 中发现了安全问题，请在 `问题列表 "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues>`__ 中提交 issue，并可选择在 "
":ref:`ArduPilot Discord 服务器 <ardupilot-discord-server>` 的 \"code_review\" "
"频道中发布该 issue 的链接。"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:105
#: b336ad3f81904feaac36c04465ef7e2d
msgid ""
"While we are keen to hear of potential security issues, before reporting, "
"please read the \"Security Attack Surface\" and \"Ground Control Station\" "
"sections above.  The most common reports we receive are from `fuzz testing "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuzzing>`__ involving changing various "
"parameters in SITL and causing the vehicle to crash or sending in invalid "
"MAVLink messages.  These are generally not valid security issues because the"
" ground station is considered trusted."
msgstr ""
"尽管我们乐于听到潜在的安全问题，但在报告之前，请先阅读上文“安全攻击面”和“地面控制站”部分。我们收到的最常见报告来自 `模糊测试 "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuzzing>`__，即在 SITL 中修改各种参数导致飞行器坠毁，或发送无效的 "
"MAVLink 消息。由于地面站被视为受信任的，这些通常不是有效的安全问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:108
#: f6fcda6661f84565aaa30ef285da22bc
msgid "Common Misconceptions"
msgstr "常见误解"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:110
#: f6b16ff6aa064ebb9ac505d6d24a906b
msgid "*\"ArduPilot is open source, so it must be insecure\"*"
msgstr "*“ArduPilot 是开源的，所以它一定不安全”*"

#: ../../source/docs/security-landing-page.rst:112
#: c9d24f307d1b41f6800335a1fb091e4d
msgid ""
"Absolutely incorrect.  The \"open\" in \"open source\" refers to the fact "
"that the source code is available for anyone to read which contributes to "
"security by having more sympathetic eyes finding and reporting issues.  This"
" does not mean that anyone can change it, nor does it mean that it must have"
" \"open\" attack surfaces.  ArduPilot's open source software is \"compiled\""
" before use (as is all C++ software), once compiled there's no fundamental "
"difference between open and closed source software.  Here are some "
"supporting articles:"
msgstr ""
"完全错误。“开源”中的“开”指的是源代码可供任何人阅读，这通过让更多善意的眼睛发现并报告问题而有助于安全。这并不意味着任何人都可以修改它，也不意味着它必须具有“开放”的攻击面。ArduPilot"
" 的开源软件在使用前会被“编译”（与所有 C++ 软件一样），一旦编译完成，开源软件与闭源软件就没有本质区别。以下是一些佐证文章："

